Rule 1 (image dtype must be floating point or integer to avoid AttributeError)
{v_1 : tensor} |= (1 ≤ dtype_(v_1) ∧ dtype_(v_1) ≤ 5) ∨ (6 ≤ dtype_(v_1) ∧ dtype_(v_1) ≤ 8)
>>
Rule 2 (for floating-point images, delta should be in (-1,1))
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : float} |= if (6 ≤ dtype_(v_1) ∧ dtype_(v_1) ≤ 8) then ((-1 < v_2) ∧ (v_2 < 1))
>>
Rule 3 (image must be at least 1D with all dimensions positive)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) ≥ 1 ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) > 0
>>
Rule 4 (if a channel dimension exists, it must be grayscale or RGB)
{v_1 : tensor} |= if ndim(v_1) ≥ 3 then (shape(v_1, ndim(v_1) - 1) = 1 ∨ shape(v_1, ndim(v_1) - 1) = 3)
>>
Rule 5 (for uint8 images, bound delta to avoid extreme shifts)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : float} |= if dtype_(v_1) = 5 then ((-255 ≤ v_2) ∧ (v_2 ≤ 255))
